ptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducable in \n- v4.5.rc2.official [2dd26a027]\n- v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.rc2 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 7600 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.13036.4) - AMD Ryzen 7 9700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.13 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe intended behaviour for `Window.start_drag()` is for the window to act as if it were being dragged on the titlebar, with the OS behaving as such. This is not the case when using a borderless window with the Windows 11 OS, though I have tested this on Linux using KDE Plasma 6 (Wayland) and it works as it should. Have not tested on Windows 10.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn a project set the window to be borderless in the project settings then call `get_window().start_drag()` from some event, say a Control button being pressed, and drag the window to the top of the screen. The Windows 11 tiling behaviour will not be triggered.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMRP not needed but here is a bare-bones project just for ease.\n\n[start_drag_bug_MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22283744/start_drag_bug_MRP.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110431/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"